# Frontend quality
- Design mobile-first with clear typographic hierarchy, intentional spacing, consistent design tokens, and meaningful focus states.
- Respect the visual direction of existing product and brand; avoid arbitrary gradients, decorative effects or generic templates.
- Use semantic HTML, landmarks, accessible labels, alt text and keyboard navigation; target WCAG 2.2 AA where applicable.
- Honor reduced motion preferences. Avoid layout shift and unnecessary animations.
- Prefer reusable components; keep state minimal. Show loading, empty, error and success states.
- Optimize image sizes, responsive srcsets, modern formats, lazy-loading and font loading.
- Check browser console, form validation, broken links and responsive layout using Playwright when available.
